<header class="content-section content-section--header">
  <div class="section-eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Privacy</div>
  <h1>Privacy &amp; data</h1>
  <p class="section-intro">This is a personal portfolio site. It collects minimal data, has no accounts, and does not sell or share your information.</p>
</header>

<div class="content-section">
  <div class="colophon-grid">
    <section aria-labelledby="priv-analytics">
      <h2 id="priv-analytics">Analytics</h2>
      <p>This site uses <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (via Google Tag Manager) to understand how visitors find and use the site — things like which pages are visited, how long people stay, and what country traffic comes from.</p>
      <p>Analytics data is aggregated and anonymous. No personally identifiable information is collected. IP addresses are anonymized by Google before storage.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="priv-cookies">
      <h2 id="priv-cookies">Cookies</h2>
      <p>This site sets a small number of cookies:</p>
      <dl class="definition-list">
        <dt><code>_ga</code></dt><dd>Google Analytics — distinguishes unique visitors. Expires after 2 years.</dd>
        <dt><code>_ga_*</code></dt><dd>Google Analytics — maintains session state. Expires after 2 years.</dd>
        <dt><code>theme</code></dt><dd>localStorage (not a cookie) — remembers your light/dark theme preference. Never sent to any server.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>No advertising, marketing, or tracking cookies are used.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="priv-third">
      <h2 id="priv-third">Third-party services</h2>
      <dl class="definition-list">
        <dt>Google Analytics</dt><dd>Pageview analytics. <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a></dd>
        <dt>Google Fonts</dt><dd>Typefaces loaded from Google's CDN. Google may log font requests. <a href="https://developers.google.com/fonts/faq/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Fonts privacy</a></dd>
        <dt>GitHub Pages</dt><dd>Site hosting. GitHub may log access for security purposes. <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub's privacy statement</a></dd>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="priv-optout">
      <h2 id="priv-optout">Opting out</h2>
      <p>You can limit data collection in several ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a></li>
        <li>Enable "Do Not Track" in your browser settings</li>
        <li>Use a content blocker that filters analytics scripts</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
